-    <title>16. Tentative conclusion</title>
+    <title>Tentative conclusion</title>
     <para>The exact ramifications of the indicator system in actual usage =
are unknown. There has never been anything like it in natural language befo=
re. The system provides great potential for emotional expression and transc=
ription, from which significant Sapir-Whorf effects can be anticipated. Whe=
n communicating across cultural boundaries, where different indicators are =
often used for the same emotion, accidental offense can be avoided. If we e=
ver ran into an alien race, a culturally neutral language of emotion could =
be vital. (A classic example, taken from the science fiction of Larry Niven=
, is to imagine speaking Lojban to the carnivorous warriors called Kzinti, =
noting that a human smile bares the teeth, and could be seen as an intent t=
o attack.) And for communicating emotions to computers, when we cannot iden=
tify all of the signals involved in subliminal human communication (things =
like body language are also cultural), a system like this is needed.</para>
